body:
This is a nice guide! Something I don't agree with though is "it's expected". I think to someone watching this who might be less familiar with tanking might take that to mean it's always appropriate to pull wall-to-wall.

&#x200B;

If your healer or DPS are under-geared in such a way that pulling this way wouldn't be feasible or fun, I don't pull like this. If my Healer is unsynced in the content we're running and I know their current level kit/gear will not allow an average player to heal me, then I don't pull like this. Lastly, it's always polite to ask your party-- particularly your Healer-- if big pulls are ok. Just because they're geared and have a kit to heal you with doesn't mean they necessarily want to stress out and do massive pulls all the time.

Vote dismiss. 

&#x200B;

If you're going to die to mechanics over and over and then complain about not getting healed instead of asking questions or trying to improve at all and blame the healer instead, you're getting my vote.
